From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 04:43:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07182/11362] [outer-loop] SGE reflect() anti-stagnation prompt
 nudge (REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3)

Picks up the documented NEXT STEP from the full-budget SGE run
(ops/known-issues.md task 6): a real g50t run showed reflect()'s
plain "what would you try differently" prompt let the model converge
on a repeated passive "wait" strategy across multiple reflection
cycles, never escalating -- the generic framing wasn't enough to
break the pattern on its own, even though the harder deterministic
collapse override (REQ-ARC-FCP-5699/5699-2) eventually escapes it.

LLMStrategyProposer.reflect() now accepts optional taboo_strategies
and computes the consecutive-null-outcome streak internally (reusing
the existing _consecutive_null_outcomes helper). When either signal
fires (streak >= _REFLECT_NUDGE_NULL_STREAK=2, deliberately softer
than the hard gate's threshold of 4), an explicit ANTI-STAGNATION
WARNING is spliced into the prompt naming the taboo strategies
verbatim and demanding a genuinely different action category.
SGECandidateRouter.rank() feeds anti_stagnation_controller.taboo_set()
into every scheduled reflect() call; reflection_nudge_fired is
recorded in last_diagnostics for auditability, matching this module's
existing convention.

11 new tests (reflect()-level nudge conditions + router-level wiring,
including a no-controller backward-compat case); one pre-existing
test updated for the legitimately-changed completer-failure return
shape. Spec: REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3 in
openspec/capabilities/arc-human-replay-frame-change/spec.md, with a
spec-declaration test matching the sibling REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-2
pattern. Not yet live-path-wired (SGECandidateRouter is still
offline-dev-only per the ARC Live-Path Reachability Discipline --
this fix strengthens the existing offline mechanism, not a new wiring
step).

